  {
   "id": "count",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 5: where does 9 come from? Let k be the number of stages and n the number of instructions."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 5 of 6: counting cycles"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "pipe"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "count"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Without a pipeline, each of the n instructions takes k cycles, so k times n: 5 times 5 is 25."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "count[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "With a pipeline, the first instruction takes k cycles to come out."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "count[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "count[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "After that, each of the other n minus 1 instructions finishes one cycle later. So k plus n minus 1: 5 plus 4 is 9."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "count[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Now take 100 instructions: 5 times 100 is 500 cycles without, and 5 plus 99 is 104 with the pipeline."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "count[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "count[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The speedup is 500 divided by 104, about 4.81."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "count[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "count[3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "As n grows, the k minus 1 cycles to fill the pipeline matter less, and the speedup approaches k, here 5."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "cycles = k + (n − 1) · speedup → k for large n"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "This ideal assumes every stage takes the same time and nothing ever has to wait. Real pipelines fall short; we see why in the next videos."
     }
    }
